{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"rao:15-3","provision":"RAO 15-3","book":"rao","book_name":"Rules of Assembly Operations","abbreviation":"RAO","reference":"15-3","title":"Section 15-3 of Article 15","supplementary":true,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/rao/15-3/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#rao/15-3","current_text":{"html":"<p class=\"lead\">The Overtures Committee shall meet immediately preceding the General Assembly in sufficient time, as determined by the Stated Clerk, for the committee to complete its work before the convening of the Assembly. Should the committee fail to finish before the convening of the Assembly, or should the committee be called into session during the meeting of the Assembly, the committee’s sessions shall be held during non-business sessions of the Assembly, unless by majority vote the Assembly directs otherwise.</p>","text":"The Overtures Committee shall meet immediately preceding the General Assembly in sufficient time, as determined by the Stated Clerk, for the committee to complete its work before the convening of the Assembly. Should the committee fail to finish before the convening of the Assembly, or should the committee be called into session during the meeting of the Assembly, the committee’s sessions shall be held during non-business sessions of the Assembly, unless by majority vote the Assembly directs otherwise."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fing